ti Cordell and several other Republicans add to a crowded GOP field, and recent coverage shows Republicans competing for Trump's endorsement while Democrats make lower-profile endorsements.\n\nPrediction markets give the Democratic ticket roughly a three percent chance, and no public polling shows a competitive race. The district lean, the money gap, and market pricing all align: this seat is expected to remain Republican by a wide margin in 2026.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -16.55}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0284, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0246, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0227, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0235, "margin": -17.0}]}